      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database is inaccessible (persistent \"Access denied\" authentication error), so I cannot run verification queries. However, I have a near-exact precedent metric (`dw_3904`) in the semantic network whose SQL matches this question's shape precisely — the only difference is that the current question asks for 9 output columns (omitting the second department name from the catalog side). I'll adapt the precedent SQL exactly, following the documented join keys, rollup logic, and window frame.\n\n**Report Summary:**\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: department dimension; `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N'), `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_CODE`.\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE**: subject code lookup; `SUBJECT_CODE`, `SUBJECT_CODE_DESC`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `SCHOOL_CODE`.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL**: extended term dimension; `TERM_CODE` (YYYYTT).\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: catalog offering per term; `SUBJECT_ID`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `TERM_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\nGraph confirms `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` joins to `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL` via TERM_CODE, and to `SIS_DEPARTMENT`/`SIS_SUBJECT_CODE`. The hint join keys match: `SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_CODE ↔ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SCHOOL_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE`.\n\n### 3–4. Precedent Evidence\n- `dw_3904` (metric): identical task shape — degree-granting subject-code rollup by school with description status ('Has Description'/'No Description', treating NULL/'nan' as missing), `GROUP BY ... WITH ROLLUP HAVING COUNT(*) > 0` for the per-school grand totals `(null, null, null, school name, null, total)`, plus 2022SU dense rank with `ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW`, joined on department name, ordered by school name, description status, total units DESC.\n- `dw_4490`: same rollup pattern with a different second subquery — confirms the rollup idiom.\n\n### 5. Coverage\nAll Phase-1 entities (4 gold tables, precedent metrics dw_3904/dw_4490, related concepts/column concepts) were retrieved and examined.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\nUse the `dw_3904` SQL verbatim, dropping only the `ic2.DEPARTMENT_NAME` column so the SELECT list has exactly the 9 requested columns in order: subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, description status, total subject codes, subject ID, total units, dense rank.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_6a988b6ecd584ccab86f8c0b",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH inner_cte1 AS (\\n  SELECT t1.SUBJECT_CODE, t1.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, t0.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t1.SCHOOL_NAME\\n  FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT t0\\n  JOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE t1 ON t0.SCHOOL_CODE = t1.SCHOOL_CODE\\n  WHERE t0.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\\n),\\nSubjectCodeVisibility AS (\\n  SELECT SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME,\\n         CASE WHEN SUBJECT_CODE_DESC IS NOT NULL AND SUBJECT_CODE_DESC <> 'nan'\\n              THEN 'Has Description' ELSE 'No Description' END AS description_status\\n  FROM inner_cte1\\n),\\nRollupResults AS (\\n  SELECT SCHOOL_NAME, description_status, COUNT(*) AS total_subject_codes\\n  FROM SubjectCodeVisibility\\n  GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME, description_status WITH ROLLUP\\n  HAVING COUNT(*) > 0\\n),\\ninner_cte2 AS (\\n  SELECT t1.SUBJECT_ID, t1.TOTAL_UNITS, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n         dense_rank() OVER (ORDER BY t1.TOTAL_UNITS ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS window_column\\n  FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL t0\\n  JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE\\n  WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2022SU'\\n)\\nSELECT scv.SUBJECT_CODE,\\n       scv.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC,\\n       scv.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n       rr.SCHOOL_NAME,\\n       rr.description_status,\\n       rr.total_subject_codes,\\n       ic2.SUBJECT_ID,\\n       ic2.TOTAL_UNITS,\\n       ic2.window_column\\nFROM RollupResults rr\\nLEFT JOIN (\\n  SELECT DISTINCT SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME, description_status\\n  FROM SubjectCodeVisibility\\n) scv ON rr.SCHOOL_NAME = scv.SCHOOL_NAME AND rr.description_status = scv.description_status\\nLEFT JOIN inner_cte2 ic2 ON scv.DEPARTMENT_NAME = ic2.DEPARTMENT_NAME\\nORDER BY rr.SCHOOL_NAME, rr.description_status, ic2.TOTAL_UNITS DESC\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
